.policy "ruff-pyi014-argument-default-in-stub" revision 2
.description "Replace complex default values of untyped parameters in stub files with an ellipsis; only simple literal defaults belong in a stub."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff PYI014 (flake8-pyi), stubs only: an unannotated parameter's default that is not a simple value (see
// python/typing's simple_value: literals, `-1`, `1 + 2j`, math and sys constants, small flat containers).
//   def f(a=os.sep, b=[[1]], c=(1, 2)): ...     ← PYI014 at `os.sep` and `[[1]]`; `(1, 2)` is fine
#include "python/typing.rr"

.violation PYI014(at: node) code "PYI014" "Replace this default value with `...`; a stub only needs to show that the parameter has a default, and keeps literal values only when they are simple."
    suppress ruff "PYI014"
PYI014(d) :- kind(f, "function_definition"), in_stub(f), sig_param(f, _, _, _, _, a, d), unset(a), !unset(d),
    !simple_value(d, "top").
